      "text": "To solve the problem, we need to determine the measure of \\(\\angle PQR\\) in degrees. We start by analyzing the given information and the geometric configuration.\n\n1. **Identify the given information:**\n   - \\(RSP\\) is a straight line.\n   - \\(\\angle QSP = 80^\\circ\\).\n\n2. **Understand the properties of a straight line:**\n   - Since \\(RSP\\) is a straight line, the sum of the angles on a straight line is \\(180^\\circ\\).\n   - Therefore, \\(\\angle SPQ + \\angle QSP = 180^\\circ\\).\n\n3. **Substitute the given value of \\(\\angle QSP\\):**\n   \\[\n   \\angle SPQ + 80^\\circ = 180^\\circ\n   \\]\n\n4. **Solve for \\(\\angle SPQ\\):**\n   \\[\n   \\angle SPQ = 180^\\circ - 80^\\circ = 100^\\circ\n   \\]\n\n5. **Determine \\(\\angle PQR\\):**\n   - Since \\(\\angle QSP\\) and \\(\\angle SPQ\\) are adjacent angles forming \\(\\angle PQR\\), we use the fact that the measures of adjacent angles that form a straight line sum to \\(180^\\circ\\).\n   - Therefore, \\(\\angle PQR = \\angle QSP + \\angle SPQ\\).\n\n6. **Substitute the known values:**\n   \\[\n   \\angle PQR = 80^\\circ + 100^\\circ = 180^\\circ - 80^\\circ = 100^\\circ\n   \\]\n\nThus, the measure of \\(\\angle PQR\\) is \\(\\boxed{100}\\).",
